The set of vectors can be represented as \(\overrightarrow{AB} = \mathbf{b}\), \(\overrightarrow{AD} = \mathbf{d}\), and \(\overrightarrow{AE} = \mathbf{e}\). The vectors \(\overrightarrow{AG}\), \(\overrightarrow{BH}\), \(\overrightarrow{CE}\), and \(\overrightarrow{DF}\) can be expressed in terms of \(\mathbf{b}\), \(\mathbf{d}\), and \(\mathbf{e}\) as follows: \[
\overrightarrow{AG} = \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e}, \quad \overrightarrow{BH} = -\mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e}, \quad \overrightarrow{CE} = \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e}, \quad \overrightarrow{DF} = \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} - \mathbf{e}
\] \] The squares of the magnitudes of these vectors are: \[
AG^2 = (\mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e}) \cdot (\mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e}) = \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} \cdot \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e} \cdot \mathbf{e} + 2 \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{d} + 2 \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{e} + 2 \mathbf{d} \cdot \mathbf{e}
\] \[
BH^2 = (-\mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e}) \cdot (-\mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e}) = \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} \cdot \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e} \cdot \mathbf{e} - 2 \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{d} - 2 \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{e} + 2 \mathbf{d} \cdot \mathbf{e}
\] \[
CE^2 = (\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e}) \cdot (\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e}) = \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} \cdot \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e} \cdot \mathbf{e} - 2 \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{d} + 2 \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{e} + 2 \mathbf{d} \cdot \mathbf{e}
\] \[
DF^2 = (\mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} - \mathbf{e}) \cdot (\mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} - \mathbf{e}) = \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} \cdot \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e} \cdot \mathbf{e} + 2 \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{d} - 2 \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{e} - 2 \mathbf{d} \cdot \mathbf{e}
\] The sum of these squares is: \[
AG^2 + BH^2 + CE^2 + DF^2 = 4 (\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{d} \cdot \mathbf{d} + \mathbf{e} \cdot \mathbf{e}) = 4 (AB^2 + AD^2 + AE^2)
